---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Submissions | The Rang Yan Review"
  description="Submission guidelines for The Rang Yan Review — poetry, fiction, essays, criticism, and interviews."
>
  <Header />

  <main id="main-content">
    <div class="container submissions-page">
      <header class="submissions-header">
        <p class="category-label">The Journal</p>
        <h1 class="submissions-title">Submission Guidelines</h1>
      </header>

      <div class="submissions-body">
        <section class="submissions-section">
          <p>
            <em>The Rang Yan Review</em> is an independent online literary journal publishing new work on a rolling basis, with each issue comprising all work published during its designated publication period.
          </p>
          <p>
            <em>The Rang Yan Review</em> welcomes original writing in English from writers, poets, critics, scholars, artists, and thinkers from anywhere in the world.
          </p>
          <p>
            We are interested in work that takes language seriously and engages critically with the world around us. We publish literature and criticism that approaches contemporary life through questions of politics, society, history, class, labour, ecology, identity, violence, memory, culture, and collective life.
          </p>
          <p>
            We are especially interested in writing that takes risks: formally, intellectually, politically, or aesthetically.
          </p>

          <h2 class="submissions-heading">What We Accept</h2>
          <p>
            We currently accept submissions in English in the following categories:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Poetry</strong> — individual poems, sequences, and longer poetic works</li>
            <li><strong>Fiction &amp; Prose</strong> — short stories, flash fiction, novel excerpts, experimental prose, and hybrid forms</li>
            <li><strong>Essays</strong> — personal, cultural, political, philosophical, and literary essays</li>
            <li><strong>Critical Writing</strong> — literary criticism, cultural criticism, theory, and essays engaging with contemporary or historical thought</li>
            <li><strong>Interviews</strong> — conversations with writers, artists, scholars, activists, and other cultural figures</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            We are open to work that crosses these categories. Hybrid, experimental, and formally unconventional submissions are very welcome.
          </p>
          <p>
            We also accept translations (with proof of permission from the original author).
          </p>

          <h2 class="submissions-heading">What We Look For</h2>
          <p>
            We value writing with a distinct voice, intellectual substance, and a genuine relationship to its subject.
          </p>
          <p>We are interested in work that:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>challenges established ways of seeing;</li>
            <li>connects individual experience with broader social and historical structures;</li>
            <li>engages seriously with political and cultural questions;</li>
            <li>experiments with literary or critical form;</li>
            <li>pays close attention to language;</li>
            <li>creates space for perspectives that are frequently marginalised or excluded from dominant cultural discourse.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            We have a particular interest in writing concerned with class, labour, capitalism, ecology, migration, colonialism, gender, sexuality, political violence, war, technology, alienation, social reproduction, collective action, and forms of resistance. These themes are invitations rather than requirements. We are equally interested in work that approaches seemingly private or intimate experience through unexpected intellectual and aesthetic perspectives.
          </p>
          <p>
            We do not expect writing to provide easy answers. Complexity, contradiction, ambiguity, and unresolved questions are welcome.
          </p>

          <h2 class="submissions-heading">Originality</h2>
          <p>
            Please submit work that you have written yourself and that you have the right to publish.
          </p>
          <p>
            Translations are welcome when the translator has the necessary rights to publish the translation. Please include the original author’s name and the original language with your submission.
          </p>
          <p>
            Previously published work may be considered in exceptional circumstances, provided that you clearly indicate where and when it was previously published.
          </p>

          <h2 class="submissions-heading">Simultaneous Submissions</h2>
          <p>
            Simultaneous submissions are welcome. If your work is accepted elsewhere, please let us know as soon as possible.
          </p>

          <h2 class="submissions-heading">Format</h2>
          <p>
            Please submit your work as a Word document (.docx) or PDF.
          </p>
          <p>
            For prose, essays, criticism, and interviews, please use a clear, readable typeface and standard formatting.
          </p>
          <p>
            For poetry, please preserve the intended lineation, spacing, and page structure of the work.
          </p>
          <p>Please include:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>your name;</li>
            <li>the title of the work;</li>
            <li>a short biographical note;</li>
            <li>your email address.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            A short cover letter is welcome, though it is not required.
          </p>

          <h2 class="submissions-heading">Length</h2>
          <p>
            There are no rigid length requirements. We care more about the quality and integrity of the work than about fitting into predetermined word counts.
          </p>
          <p>As a general guide:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Poetry:</strong> up to 10 poems or approximately 15 pages</li>
            <li><strong>Fiction &amp; Prose:</strong> up to 8,000 words</li>
            <li><strong>Essays &amp; Critical Writing:</strong> up to 8,000 words</li>
            <li><strong>Interviews:</strong> up to 8,000 words</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Longer works may be considered when their length is integral to the work itself.
          </p>

          <h2 class="submissions-heading">Editorial Approach</h2>
          <p>
            <em>The Rang Yan Review</em> is an independent, non-commercial literary project. We do not publish according to commercial trends or market expectations.
          </p>
          <p>
            We read submissions as literary and intellectual works rather than as commodities. We are interested in writing capable of creating a space for serious thought, disagreement, solidarity, and experimentation.
          </p>
          <p>
            Our editorial process is selective, and acceptance depends on the quality and relevance of the work to the journal.
          </p>
          <p>
            We aim to treat every submission with attention and respect.
          </p>

          <h2 class="submissions-heading">Payment</h2>
          <p>
            <em>The Rang Yan Review</em> is a non-profit, independent cultural project. We currently do not pay contributors for published work.
          </p>
          <p>
            The journal is maintained as a shared space for literary and intellectual exchange, outside commercial publishing structures. Our aim is to make room for writing that may have difficulty finding a place within commercially driven cultural institutions.
          </p>

          <aside class="author-rights" aria-labelledby="author-rights-heading">
            <h2 id="author-rights-heading" class="author-rights__title">Author Rights</h2>
            <p>
              Authors retain copyright to their work. By submitting work to <em>The Rang Yan Review</em>, authors grant the journal the non-exclusive right to publish the accepted work in the journal, on its website, and in its digital archives.
            </p>
            <p>
              Authors retain the right to republish their work elsewhere after publication in <em>The Rang Yan Review</em>, provided that the journal is acknowledged as the first place of publication.
            </p>
            <p>
              Submission and publication do not constitute a transfer of copyright to <em>The Rang Yan Review</em>.
            </p>
            <p>
              Authors are responsible for ensuring that their submissions are original and that they have the necessary rights and permissions for any material incorporated into their work.
            </p>
          </aside>

          <h2 class="submissions-heading">How to Submit</h2>
          <p>
            Please send your submission to
            <a href="mailto:sensus.interni@gmail.com">sensus.interni@gmail.com</a>
            with the subject line:
          </p>
          <p class="submissions-example">
            SUBMISSION — [Your Name] — [Category]
          </p>
          <p>For example:</p>
          <p class="submissions-example">
            SUBMISSION — Jane Smith — Poetry
          </p>
          <p>
            Please send your work as a single attachment whenever possible.
          </p>
          <p>
            We look forward to reading your work.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .submissions-page {
    padding: 4rem 0 0;
  }

  .submissions-header {
    margin-bottom: 3.5rem;
    padding-bottom: 2rem;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--color-ink);
    max-width: 60ch;
  }

  .submissions-header .category-label {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .submissions-title {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.75rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    margin: 0;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .submissions-body {
    max-width: 68ch;
  }

  .submissions-section p {
    font-family: var(--font-serif-body);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.85;
    color: var(--color-ink-secondary);
    margin-bottom: 1em;
  }

  .submissions-section p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .submissions-section em {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .submissions-section strong {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .submissions-section a {
    color: var(--color-burgundy);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 0.15em;
  }

  .submissions-section a:hover {
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .submissions-section ul {
    margin: 0 0 1.25em;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }

  .submissions-section li {
    font-family: var(--font-serif-body);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--color-ink-secondary);
    margin-bottom: 0.45em;
  }

  .submissions-heading {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    margin: 2.5rem 0 1rem;
    padding-top: 0.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .submissions-example {
    font-family: var(--font-sans) !important;
    font-size: 0.95rem !important;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--color-ink) !important;
    background: var(--color-paper-dark);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--color-burgundy);
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    margin: 1rem 0 1.25rem !important;
  }

  .author-rights {
    background: #fff;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    padding: 1.7rem 1.75rem 1.45rem;
    margin: 2.5rem 0 0.5rem;
  }

  .author-rights__title {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }

  .author-rights p {
    font-family: var(--font-serif-body);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.85;
    color: var(--color-ink-secondary);
    margin: 0 0 1em;
  }

  .author-rights p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .author-rights em {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
</style>
